Gaulle Bernard writes:

 > Do we consider that we need to change a well known environment syntax for
 > an obsolate manner of inputing accented letters? In few years (i hope)
 > nobody will use the old Knuth manner for putting diacritics and everybody
 > will input (at least) 8bits chars and then we will discuss about the 32bits
 > notation...

I agree with Bernard as far as european languages are concerned.
However, for, say, oriental languages (and I think that is what
Dominik is concerned about), I doubt that we will be able to live
without the accent commands.

Another point to consider here is the user interface. I think that it
wasn't a good idea in the first place that \' and \` mean something
different inside the tabbing environment.

